        "  - Scree plot for PCA with corresponding commulative variance explained. And 2-dimensional plots for t-SNE to visualize separation and overlap between introvert and extrovert.\n",
        "- **Interpretation**:\n",
        "  - For PCA, we have found that we need 5 principal components to explain 85% of the variance from our dataset. This means that the features or columns of our dataset are not redundant, and the information is spread across several different dimensions of behavior.\n",
        "  - For t-SNE, there is a distinct spatial separation between the two targets. This suggests that the behavioral features we've selected (post frequency, interaction types, response times, etc.) are strong predictors of personality type. Clustering indicates that users within the same category share very similar behavioral patterns in the high-dimensional space.\n",
